    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d211">

                <pb facs="0274" n="250" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg250"/>

                <head>Mr. Sanford to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 183.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 25, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi>The Moniteur of the 23d instant publishes
                    the tables of the “indirect” revenue of the state for the year 1863 compared
                    with the revenues from similar sources in 1862.</p>
                <p>The total in 1863 amounts to 116,750,364 francs, being an augmentation of
                    2,860,465 francs upon that of 1862, and about five and one-half million francs
                    more than the estimates.</p>
                <p>This increase arises principally from spirits, beer, and vinegar, inheritances,
                    stamps, railroads, and telegraphs. There is a diminution in receipts from
                    customs, registry, conveyances, and steam lines between Ostend and Dover.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. S. SANFORD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State,</hi> &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.,
                            &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
